us_drifts) can be polluted under reordering if an earlier test already recorded the same status. Non-manifesting today (CI runs the full suite green in definition order), purely defensive. Fix: add an autouse fixture calling outbound_mapper.reset_drift_warnings() before each test in the module. Test-only, behavior-preserving. Filed for follow-up.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","3d7a-7795-efde-4df7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"3d7a-7795-efde-4df7","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ab9f-e9ba-de24-48bd","ticket_type":"task","title":"Add autouse fixture resetting _DRIFT_WARNED for status-mapping tests","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4d59af5e-1290-456e-8b1a-36fcab731753","4e694bf4-2650-4fb5-83b2-ab97dfaec953"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787346206258939001,"uuid":"4113d8f9-f1fc-4ad0-9822-6fad8515ad33"}